        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "8dc5efd2-33d7-5be8-840d-31fa6ba76f31",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: Cave Rock Tunnel, Stateline, Douglas County, Nevada, Lake Tahoe\n- Roads: U.S. Route 50\n- Peoples: Washoe, Paiute\n- Creatures/Legends: Tahoe Tessie\n\nFacts:\n- In the mid-19th century, members of the Washoe and Paiute tribes told stories that a lake-dwelling creature now known as Tahoe Tessie lives in an underwater tunnel beneath Cave Rock.\n- Sightings of Tahoe Tessie have continued into modern times.\n- Cave Rock Tunnel is a dual-bore highway tunnel on U.S. Route 50 along the eastern shore of Lake Tahoe in Douglas County, Nevada, about seven miles north of Stateline.\n- Stateline, Nevada, had a population of 842 in the 2010 census.",
